{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjFpCPnqzQMpknxSFan5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016rprz53WcXe7n8KUhkAGhr","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"Start: D4 quarter just below the staff, then a quarter rest, then a barline. That is bar 89 (D4 quarter, rest). It is not the end of bar 88, which would have a G4 8th, D4 quarter and D4 8th. Next comes a rest and a sharped F4, which is bar 90 (rest, F#4). Then G4 and a rest, which is bar 91. Then a rest and F#4, which is bar 92. Then G4 and a rest, which is bar 93. Then a quarter rest, an 8th rest and a G4 8th, which is bar 94. Then G4 and F#4, each a quarter with tremolo strokes, which is bar 95 (repeated 16ths). Then a G4+G3 double stop below the staff and a rest, which is bar 96. After the next barline comes a beamed figure: a small grace note, then G5 F#5 G5 (sharp on the F). A second identical figure follows. Together they are bar 97, the edition's two grace + G5-F#5-G5 groups. A third identical figure, with its own grace note and accidental, comes before the end of the staff. It seems to follow a faint barline. Bar 97 holds only two such figures, so this third one is the first half of bar 98. The next line would finish that bar. So the line holds bars 89 to 98, not 89 to 97.","right":false,"insights":"Bars 89–96 were easy to match. They have distinct rests, sharps, the tremolo bar and the low double stop. The ending was hard because bars 97–100 repeat the same grace + G5-F#5-G5 figure, and the barline before the last figure is faint. Counting figures against the edition's two per bar settled it. A sharper image of the end of the staff, or a barline count from the program, would make this certain."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5403,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5